# Build context for docker/app.Dockerfile (context: the repository root).
#
# Two reasons this file matters more than usual here:
#
#  1. `node_modules/` is ~400 MB of host-installed, host-linked packages. pnpm
#     uses symlinks into a store that does not exist inside the image, so
#     shipping it would not even work — the image installs its own closure in
#     the `prod-deps` stage.
#  2. A stale `dist/` from the host would be COPYed over whatever the `build`
#     stage produced, and the image would then run code nobody built in it.
#     That is the exact failure DOCKER.md §5 exists to prevent, arriving by
#     the back door.
#
# Everything else here is transfer time on a 4-core shared machine.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.turbo
**/.turbo
.cache
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
docker/fakes
infra
runbooks
docs
.github
scripts/negative-tests
